Description: Hide the mouse cursor while typing on Wayland, like xbanish
 wbanish hides the mouse cursor when a key is pressed, and shows it again when
 the mouse is moved, a button is pressed or the wheel is scrolled. It is a
 Wayland counterpart of xbanish. It works on GNOME through its bundled GNOME
 Shell extension, and on compositors that implement the wlr-layer-shell
 protocol, where the user has to be in the "input" group.

